## 12. Troubleshooting Notes

### No email received

- Check that the SNS email subscription is confirmed.
- Check spam or junk folders.
- Verify the SNS topic ARN and Region.
- Review the Lambda execution logs.

### Lambda did not run after upload

- Verify that the S3 trigger is enabled.
- Confirm that the correct bucket is configured.
- Check the S3 event type.
- Review Lambda permissions and CloudWatch logs.

### Access denied errors

Review the Lambda execution role and ensure it has the required permissions to read the S3 objects and publish to the SNS topic.

### Incorrect word count

Check the text file contents and remember that `split()` separates words using whitespace. Punctuation attached to a word does not count as a separate word.

## 13. Security and Improvements

- Use least-privilege IAM permissions.
- Keep the S3 bucket private.
- Never publish AWS credentials or sensitive account information.
- Consider handling events containing multiple S3 records.
- Add error handling for invalid text files and missing objects.
- Consider duplicate event processing when designing production workflows.

## 14. Conclusion

This project demonstrated how Amazon S3, AWS Lambda, Amazon SNS, IAM, and CloudWatch can work together to create a serverless automation workflow.

Two test uploads successfully triggered the function and generated email notifications with the correct word counts.
